> 
> This script compares and integrates economic damage estimates due to climate change for the UK, using data from both COACCH and CCRA3 projects. It begins by processing data from a CSV file, accommodating missing channels using methodologies like Nordhaus’s. The script simulates 1000 Monte Carlo samples to assess variance across different damage estimation channels. Double-count adjustments are made for droughts, and results are aggregated by year and channel. Data from CCRA3 is also processed, cleaned, and integrated. The GDP growth rate is calculated to project future economic damages as a percentage of GDP. The script then prepares the combined dataset for plotting, focusing on baseline and high mitigation scenarios. Using ggplot2, it visualizes the economic damages by various impact channels over time. Changes for the final presentation include highlighting specific sectors and reorganizing scenarios. Results are saved to a PDF file.
